  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday Night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1111 AM CDT Thu Apr 16 2026\n\nOn Saturday, another trough will be taking shape to our west, and \nthis one has a strong cold front associated with it. As this system \nmoves through, it will result in high rain chances across the area. \nModels continue to suggest that most of the activity will be behind \nthe front. That's more good news as it means that our severe weather \nthreat is very low, and even the threat for lightning may be low as \nwell. While we need this rain, the rain today and into Saturday \nwon't amount to much. Between the two systems, rain amounts are \nstill expected to be below one inch with low probabilities of 10-20% \nof getting more than one inch. So enough rain to get the ground wet,\nbut not enough to start putting a dent in the severe drought that\nhas now developed across most of Middle TN.\n\nBehind Saturday's cold front, temperatures will cool with highs on \nSunday in the 60s and then warming into the 70s Monday and Tuesday. \nBut temperatures will climb back into the low-80s by the middle of \nnext week. As far as rain goes, there doesn't look to be much of it \nas we head into next week as the pattern favors only low rain \nchances toward the end of next week.",
